---
source: crates/specforge-cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Validate .spec files and report diagnostics

Usage: specforge check [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          Path to the spec root directory
          
          [default: .]

Options:
      --strict
          Promote warnings to errors

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

      --lint <LINT>
          Extra lint profiles: inferred (I200/I202 from specforge-infer.json); pedantic is the default and adds nothing
          
          [possible values: inferred, pedantic]

      --severity <SEVERITY>
          Show only diagnostics of this severity (after --strict); the exit code and --cache still judge everything reported
          
          [possible values: error, warning, info]

      --cache
          Record each entity's lifecycle state (e.g. a feature's status) in specforge-cache.json when the check passes (the build cache history rules compare against)

  -h, --help
          Print help
